From 3fde9a904610ee3cbb332568a30aa19a840da12c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] gateway: late session inventory follows its reply, a
 failed build settles, classic CLI prints its notices

Follow-up to PR #2198 (review 5891116059, three non-blocking points).

1. Ordering. A build finishing while a pending create/resume reply was still being assembled
   (the transcript read) published session.info before the reply: Ink dropped it on create (sid
   unknown yet) and a resume reply's pending shape overwrote the merged inventory (banner stuck at
   "..."). AuthorityConnection.dispatch now runs handlers under reply_scoped(): a reply that
   carried inventory_pending takes a hold on the shared build, released with loop.call_soon after
   the handler returns. The transport queues the reply in that same pass (write_async takes its
   send lock at once or waits in its FIFO), so the late session.info is always behind it.
2. Failure. A build failing inside the budget answered pending with nothing ever published; one
   failing after it only logged. Now the in-budget reply carries the settled empty shape
   (inventory_pending: false, empty sections), and a failure after a pending reply publishes that
   shape as session.info.
3. Classic CLI. While pending, unknown_toolsets and tool_availability_warnings never printed (only
   from the startup reply). SessionState gains info_listeners; _adopt_gateway_toolsets waits for
   the settled session.info, prints them once and keeps it as the snapshot's banner info.
   /reload-mcp counts tools from the full session.info RPC, not a resume reply that can be the
   pending shape (0 tools).

Proof:
- RED on base 82d31e6c5d: test_late_inventory_reaches_the_viewer_only_after_the_reply (info
  before 'reply'), test_a_build_failing_after_the_budget_publishes_a_settled_empty_inventory
  (no frame), test_a_build_failing_inside_the_budget_answers_settled_not_pending (pending True),
  test_late_inventory_prints_the_startup_notices_once (nothing printed),
  test_reload_mcp_runs_on_the_gateway (session.resume, 0 tools).
- GREEN: those plus 255 test files / 2022 tests importing the touched modules
  (session_local_inventory, session_controls/AuthorityConnection, gateway_connection,
  cli_init_mixin); scripts/check ruff ok.
